      "date": "1900s",
      "kind": "site history",
      "description": "Developed by Sol Getz & Son, the realty firm that graded and sold much of the north-western Oceanside. Getz would level a block, lease the flat lots on terms requiring the tenant to build within a set period, then sell the property to that tenant within the year.",
